  unitName: Gortius, Elysia's Crown
  unitId: 810908
  unitNumber: 8627
  description: "Crown Prince Gortius, though eldest son of King Radmuhl and next
    in line for the Elysian throne, much preferred running drills in the courtyard
    with his men than debate nobles in court. Where his younger sister Estia studied
    the comforting mystique of the Light, Gortius spent his formative years chasing
    dreams of gallant heroism.Upon his twenty-fifth summer, Gortius personally mounted
    a bold offensive against the Northern pirates. Though the Northern Campaign was
    a resounding success, it was said to have cost Gortius his life, forever lost
    beneath the waves. All Elysia mourned their Crown Prince, but none was more aggrieved
    than his father\u2014the sorrow of which would eventually claim the old king's
    life.In truth, Gortius had secretly fled from the burdens of eventual kingship
    with Miriam, his half-Alethi second in command. The frozen steppes of Eiros served
    as the backdrop of their idyllic life for some five winters\u2014as well as the
    birthplace of their daughter, Evgenia.Fate would soon catch up with the prince,
    however, when troubles at home forced Gortius to return to Elysia. Reasonably
    just toward friend and foe alike, Gortius's kindness was a liability in the mire
    of his court, a shortcoming that Miriam was eager to compensate with lethal judgement.
    As much as Gortius loved his family, the stresses of rulership caught up with
    them, forever changing the once-happy family\u2014and culminating in his quiet
    demise.Though detractors declare him the end of House Valen, others agree Gortius's
    spirit still lives on in Evgenia, whose burning resolve shines through her defiant
    eyes and carries the torch of her father for the long years ahead."
  summonDesc: "Once a prince, ever a prince.<br>I've returned\u2014for good this
    time.<br>My duty is to Elysia, after all."
  fusionDesc: Well done, soldier.<br>I dare say you've earned yourself some high
    praise!<br>Ha ha!
  evoDesc: Weary is the head that bears the crown...
  element: 1
  rarity: 7
